# Visualization docs

Interactive figures live in `index.html`. Each has a living doc under `visualizations/`.

## Before editing a viz

1. Identify which figure (see `visualizations/README.md`).
2. **Read** that figure’s `.md` file first.
3. Prefer matching existing controls, camera, and physics conventions documented there.

## After editing a viz

1. Update the matching `visualizations/<name>.md` (behavior, DOM ids, defaults, changelog date).
2. Update root `MEMORY.md` if controls, physics constants, removed figures, or scope changed.
3. Vault figure blocks only sync **cap / title / hint** — do not invent new `:::figure` ids without apply/export awareness.

## Current figures

`flow`, `kick`, `wind`, `ce`, `galaxy`, `micro`, plus page-level **lens** gag (`data-effect="lens"`) — `#demo` demographics stack is removed.

## Themes

Site themes are `light` / `dark` only. Canvas/SVG draws should use `vizColors()` / `--viz-*` (not hard-coded paper/stage hexes) so dark mode recolors figures. Theme switches call `refreshThemeVisuals()`.
